      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A chronic clinical course for intussusception of the bowel in children is an unusual, but well recognized phenomenon. We report a case of a young child whose symptoms of vomiting and abdominal pains continued for over a month before radiological investigation made the diagnosis of ileocolic intussusception which was then successfully reduced by air enema."},
